  "hypothesis": "H: A fresh typed health observation below the current authored hard minimum during a pending planner turn yields policy invalidation; the current V39 cancellation helper sends executor cancel before planner interruption, and an owner-backed Xvfb keyup is observed before the completed planner answer can be admitted.",
  "test": "T: Two arms at source seq2/current seq3 with identical binding and retained frame: synthetic health=80 (source 97, authored max loss 8, hard minimum 89) and unchanged health=97 control. Each starts current-main InputOwner V4/V12, focuses an Xvfb client, holds key a, and begins a pending PersistentPlannerAdapter turn. The production DoomCoverSignalPairMonitor and cancel_invalidated_cover helper are AST-extracted from frozen current-main source. A minimal executor protocol peer translates the exact production cancel message to owner.call(up_batch); the real Xvfb server and independent observer verify keyup. One candidate invocation total; no game/model/physical input.",
  "decision": "D: PASS_METHOD_SCOPED only if hard-drop arm produces health hard invalidation, cancel message before planner interrupt, verified owner keyup and independent KeyRelease before completed answer is observed, planner marks answer ineligible/cancellation requested, final action admission rejects policy invalidation with no Executor admission; unchanged control has no invalidation/cancel, eligible planner answer, READY_FOR_FRESH_EXECUTOR_ADMISSION, key held until owner cleanup, and Xvfb exits 0. STOP on runtime, release, ordering, or cleanup mismatch.",
  "confounds": "C: Health=80 is synthetic typed telemetry from retained seq3, not a measured game event; fake executor consumes the real protocol cancel and invokes the actual current owner up_batch API, but does not run the production executor subprocess. Fake planner returns a deterministic completed answer; this intentionally tests stale-answer race handling, not model semantics.",
